{"author":{"id":"746a4d30afc20b78119cb8ed7c194f988174fc252f0e9d9eb92022244ef86db3"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1779504051,"nonce":"bImrgndd6j4jTPmPmDnOrKNBTO0=","metadata":{"github-id":"I_kwDOK4fCvM8AAAABDJz6kg","github-url":"https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/162","origin":"github"},"title":"Battery annunciator stays green at \u003cBATT_LOW_VOLT — threshold-to-color mapping broken","message":"## Symptom\n\nDuring [#160](https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/160) (2026-05-22 deployment) the **Battery annunciator row stayed green from session start through recovery**, even with battery mean voltage well below FCU `BATT_LOW_VOLT = 23.0 V` for many minutes (down to ~22 V loaded, ~22.43 V at charger-connect). The row was **displaying live voltage** the entire time — the data path is intact; only the threshold-to-color mapping is broken.\n\nThis is **class-blocking** for the June 2026 Summer Hydro deployment: students cannot be expected to monitor `mavros/battery` raw voltage in real time. The annunciator is the operator's safety contract. Mitigation today was operator-manual voltage monitoring + early recovery, which worked but is not viable with students at the controls.\n\n## Diagnosis path\n\nLoaded config (verified at wrap-up):\n\n```yaml\n# bizzyboat_project11/config/bizzyboat_annunciator.yaml:35\n- name: Battery\n  source: diagnostics\n  diagnostic_name: \"mavros: Battery\"\n  format: \"{}\"\n```\n\nOperator observation contradicts salmon log §7's \"DiagnosticStatus missing from `/diagnostics`\" diagnosis — if `mavros: Battery` were truly absent from the bus, the voltage value wouldn't render. Salmon's `/diagnostics` capture likely missed the publish window (mavros publishes at ~1 Hz).\n\nMost likely root cause: **the `level` field of `mavros: Battery`'s `DiagnosticStatus` stays at `OK` (0) regardless of voltage**. mavros' `sys_status` plugin only escalates battery `level` when its own `min_voltage` parameter is set; if the boat-side mavros config doesn't configure those thresholds, the level stays OK forever and the annunciator (which presumably colors by `DiagnosticStatus.level`) stays green.\n\n## Candidate fixes (to be investigated)\n\n1. **Configure mavros `sys_status.min_voltage`** (and similar) to match FCU `BATT_LOW_VOLT = 23.0 V` and `BATT_CRT_VOLT = 21.5 V` so the diagnostic level escalates correctly.\n2. **Switch the annunciator's Battery row source** from `diagnostics` → direct subscription to `/bizzy/mavros/battery` with thresholds evaluated in the annunciator (decouples from mavros plugin config).\n3. **Use a different DiagnosticStatus producer** that already tracks the FCU's `BATTERY_STATUS` low-voltage flags directly.\n\nPick whichever makes the chain most robust against future regressions. Option 1 is the smallest change; option 2 owns the thresholds in our code.\n\n## Verification\n\nAfter fix:\n- At voltage \u003c 23.0 V sustained 10 s (matching `BATT_LOW_TIMER`), annunciator row goes yellow.\n- At voltage \u003c 21.5 V sustained 10 s, annunciator row goes red.\n- At voltage \u003e 23.0 V, row green.\n- Behavior holds after mavros restart.\n\n## Context\n\n- Originating deployment: #160 (2026-05-22)\n- Dev log: `docs/logs/2026/2026-05-22_dev_logs.md` — \"🚨 Annunciator confirmed silent at 22 V — DEFINITIVE BUG\" + integration entry correcting salmon §7\n- Salmon log: `docs/logs/2026/2026-05-22_salmon_logs.md` §7 (note: §7's \"DiagnosticStatus missing\" diagnosis was incomplete — see corrected dev-log entry)\n- FCU params today: `BATT_LOW_VOLT=23.0`, `BATT_CRT_VOLT=21.5`, `BATT_LOW_TIMER=10`, `BATT_FS_LOW_ACT=0`, `BATT_FS_CRT_ACT=0` (annunciator-only, no autopilot action)\n- Hard deadline: dev freeze 2026-06-04 (Summer Hydro class start)\n\nPart of #160.\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context)`","files":null}]}